<odoo>
    <!--
        Keeps the support queue seated with today's agents.

        Every support conversation seats its agents when it opens and again
        whenever the visitor comes back to it, so this is not the main path —
        it is the one that covers the conversation nobody has reopened. Grant
        somebody the support group this morning and by tonight they are in
        every waiting conversation, including the ones opened before they were
        appointed.

        Nightly rather than hourly: appointing an agent is a rare, deliberate
        act, and the two immediate paths already cover the common case. A
        frequent job here would spend its time re-reading a queue that has not
        changed.
    -->
    <record id="ir_cron_support_sync_agents" model="ir.cron">
        <field name="name">Chat: sentar a los agentes de soporte en las conversaciones abiertas</field>
        <field name="model_id" ref="mail.model_discuss_channel" />
        <field name="state">code</field>
        <field name="code">model._support_sync_agents()</field>
        <field name="interval_number">1</field>
        <field name="interval_type">days</field>
        <field name="active" eval="True" />
    </record>

    <!--
        Support conversations are temporary on purpose.

        Left alone they become two bad things at once: a queue nobody can read,
        because a hundred finished conversations sit among the three that are
        waiting; and a permanent archive of strangers' messages, which is more
        than we were given and more than we need.

        So a conversation that has gone quiet is CLOSED (3 days), and a closed
        one is DELETED (7 days, or 30 for a visitor who told us their name).
        Reopening is free: writing again clears the flag.

        Daily rather than weekly, with the windows expressed in days: the
        retention is what the visitor was promised, and running the sweep more
        often than that only makes it land closer to the promise. All three
        windows are system parameters, so widening them needs no deploy.
    -->
    <record id="ir_cron_support_gc" model="ir.cron">
        <field name="name">Chat: cerrar y borrar las conversaciones de soporte antiguas</field>
        <field name="model_id" ref="mail.model_discuss_channel" />
        <field name="state">code</field>
        <field name="code">model._support_gc()</field>
        <field name="interval_number">1</field>
        <field name="interval_type">days</field>
        <field name="nextcall" eval="(DateTime.now().replace(hour=4, minute=30, second=0) + timedelta(days=1)).strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')" />
        <field name="active" eval="True" />
    </record>
</odoo>
